{"seq": 23, "ts": "2026-11-12T09:55:16.664Z", "run_id": "run-20261112-095441-4be54b", "session": "sess-reviewer", "agent": "reviewer", "role": "reviewer", "event": "review", "task": "collect", "verdict": "changes_requested", "defects": [{"file": "pipeline/collect.py", "why": "The CLI does not create the parent directory of --out when it is missing; main() opens args.out directly with open(args.out, 'w'), which raises FileNotFoundError if the parent directory does not exist."}, {"file": "pipeline/collect.py", "why": "Fetch/parse failures are not reported loudly. _fetch exceptions propagate as tracebacks but there is no explicit error handling; more importantly, a page whose table yields no records (or a row whose value cell fails float() and is silently skipped) produces fewer records with exit 0 and no error message, violating the requirement to fail loudly instead of silently producing fewer records."}, {"file": "pipeline/collect.py", "why": "The module docstring does not state the contract (input shape, output record shape, no filtering); it only says 'Collector: fetch site pages and parse table#readings into records.'"}], "round": 1}
