{"seq": 56, "ts": "2026-11-12T09:55:57.297Z", "run_id": "run-20261112-095441-4be54b", "session": "sess-reviewer", "agent": "reviewer", "role": "reviewer", "event": "review", "task": "analyze", "verdict": "changes_requested", "defects": [{"file": "pipeline/analyze.py", "why": "by_site is emitted as a dict keyed by site and sorted by site name ascending, not sorted by (-total, site) as the checklist requires; the docstring also states 'sorted by key (ascending, plain string sort)'. The required fields site,total,mean,device_count,kept_count are also absent (only count,total,mean are produced)."}, {"file": "pipeline/analyze.py", "why": "top_devices entries lack the required 'site' and 'mean' fields (only device,count,total are emitted), and ordering is by (-total, device) rather than (-total, site, device)."}, {"file": "pipeline/analyze.py", "why": "mean is computed as round(total/kept_count) using the unrounded raw total, not the rounded total as the checklist requires; the docstring also says rounding is applied only at emit time on raw sums."}, {"file": "pipeline/store.py", "why": "records table uses an AUTOINCREMENT id primary key instead of PK(site,device,day); the checklist requires records PK(site,device,day)."}, {"file": "pipeline/analyze.py", "why": "The docstring does not state the required filter/rounding/ordering/tie-break rules correctly: it documents by_site/by_device as sorted by key ascending and top_devices as (-total, device), contradicting the required (-total, site) and (-total, site, device) orderings, and does not document the mean-from-rounded-total rule."}], "round": 1}
